			<li>The general support and information we publish &mdash; release notes, documentation at <code>vectismail.com/getting-started</code>, and the like.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>They <strong>do not</strong> cover:</p>
		<ul style="line-height: 1.8;">
			<li><strong>The software licence for Vectis Mail itself.</strong> That's the Business Source License 1.1 ("BSL"), included with the source at <a href="https://github.com/Veltara-Works/vectis/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">github.com/Veltara-Works/vectis/blob/main/LICENSE</a>. The BSL determines what you can do with the source code, with the binaries we build from it, and when each version converts to Apache License 2.0 (four years from each version's first public release). These Terms do not modify the BSL; the BSL prevails on any question about source-code rights.</li>
