			<li><strong>Your relationship with your own users.</strong> Vectis Mail is a self-hosted product. Once you've installed it, you operate it. Your end-users (the people whose mailboxes you host) are your responsibility, not ours.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>By using vectismail.com or by holding a Vectis Pro subscription, you agree to these Terms. If you don't agree, please don't use the site or buy the product.</p>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">2. Who we are</h2>
		<p>Vectis Mail is a product of Veltara Works, an Australian operation. The principal contact is the founder, Ian Holt. Contact: <a href="mailto:support@vectismail.com" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">support@vectismail.com</a>.</p>
		<p>"We", "us", "our" in this document means Veltara Works. "You", "your" means you, the person or organisation reading these Terms and using the site or subscription.</p>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">3. Using vectismail.com</h2>

		<h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">3a. What you can do</h3>
		<p>Browse the site. Read the docs. Copy code from the documentation into your own projects (it's there for you to use). Link to any page on the site from anywhere. Quote and excerpt content (with a fair citation back to the source). Submit the contact form when you have a question.</p>

		<h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">3b. What we ask you not to do</h3>
		<p>Please don't:</p>
		<ul style="line-height: 1.8;">
			<li>Scrape the site at volume in a way that could affect its availability to other visitors. Reasonable, well-behaved crawling (robots.txt-respecting) is fine.</li>
			<li>Use automated tooling to flood the contact form, submit fake enquiries, or impersonate someone else.</li>
			<li>Attempt to interfere with, probe, exploit, or otherwise abuse the site's infrastructure. If you're doing security research and you've found something interesting, please report it to <a href="mailto:support@vectismail.com" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">support@vectismail.com</a> with "Security" in the subject &mdash; we'll happily acknowledge the finding.</li>
