			<li>Frame the site, mirror it, or republish it in a way that misrepresents authorship.</li>
		</ul>

		<h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">3c. Site availability</h3>
		<p>We aim to keep vectismail.com available, but we don't guarantee 100% uptime. The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages; from time to time we may take it down for maintenance, redesign, or in response to incidents. We don't owe you anything for downtime on the marketing site.</p>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">4. Vectis Mail subscriptions (Pro tier)</h2>

		<h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">4a. The relationship</h3>
		<p>A Vectis Pro subscription is a commercial agreement that consists of three pieces, intentionally:</p>
		<ol style="line-height: 1.8;">
			<li>Veltara Works is the licensor of the software (under the BSL).</li>
			<li>ValidonX is the merchant of record and the entity that bills you.</li>
			<li>You are the operator who installs and runs Vectis Mail on infrastructure you control.</li>
		</ol>
		<p>A subscription buys you the right to run Vectis Mail in production for your organisation (and the end-users of your organisation) under the terms of the BSL's Additional Use Grant. One subscription covers all Vectis Mail installs operated by your organisation. Each $29 USD per month invoice covers one tenant for one calendar month.</p>

		<h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">4b. What the subscription includes</h3>
		<ul style="line-height: 1.8;">
			<li>Pro feature unlocks on your install (unlimited domains, unlimited mailboxes, per-domain analytics, OIDC SSO, custom branding, advanced spam controls, and other capabilities as listed at <a href="/pricing" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">/pricing</a>).</li>
			<li>Priority email support, routed through <code>support@vectismail.com</code>.</li>
			<li>Access to stable releases and the right to apply them in production.</li>
		</ul>

		<h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">4c. What it doesn't include</h3>
		<ul style="line-height: 1.8;">
			<li>Hosting. You bring your own infrastructure (a Linux VPS, your own bare metal, your own cloud account).</li>
			<li>Migration services from another mail platform. We're happy to advise and many customers migrate themselves, but full white-glove migration is a separately-quoted engagement.</li>
			<li>Custom feature development. Feature requests are welcome on GitHub and we triage them as they come in, but a paid subscription does not entitle you to a specific feature on a specific timeline. If you need a feature on a contractual SLA, talk to us about an enterprise engagement.</li>
			<li>Indemnity for content your end-users send. You are the operator of your mail server; you bear primary responsibility for the content that passes through it.</li>
		</ul>

		<h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">4d. Billing, renewals, cancellations</h3>
		<p>All of this is handled by ValidonX. In short:</p>
		<ul style="line-height: 1.8;">
			<li>Subscriptions auto-renew monthly until you cancel them through the billing portal at <code>/account/billing</code>.</li>
			<li>Cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period; you keep Pro feature access until then and your Vectis Mail install falls back to the Starter tier afterwards. Your data is not locked &mdash; the mail server continues to run mail.</li>
			<li>If a payment fails, you have a 21-day grace period during which Pro features continue to work while we and ValidonX attempt to collect. After that, the install enters a "past due" state and Pro features are restricted; the core mail server continues to operate so you do not lose mail.</li>
			<li>Refunds: ValidonX administers refunds in line with Australian Consumer Law. If something has gone genuinely wrong on our side and you've paid for a service you couldn't use, write to us and we'll work with ValidonX to make it right.</li>
		</ul>

		<h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">4e. Resale and managed-hosting</h3>
		<p>Vectis Mail is licensed under the BSL. The Additional Use Grant covers running the software for your own organisation and your own end-users (including delivering mail for customers of your organisation, e.g. an agency hosting mail for its design clients). It <strong>does not</strong> permit you to offer Vectis Mail itself to third parties on a hosted, embedded, or managed-service basis in a way that competes with Veltara Works's paid offering. If you want to do that, email <a href="mailto:licensing@veltaraworks.com" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">licensing@veltaraworks.com</a> and we'll discuss a separate arrangement.</p>

